    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Key Relationships\n\n### Internal Energy\nFor an ideal gas: **du = c_v dT**\n\n### Enthalpy\nFor an ideal gas: **dh = c_p dT**\n\n### Specific Heat Relationship\nFor an ideal gas: **c_p - c_v = R**\n\nwhere R is the individual gas constant\n\n### Ratio of Specific Heat\n**k = c_p / c_v**\n\nwhere:\n- k = Ratio of Specific Heat (dimensionless)\n- c_p = specific heat at constant pressure (kJ/kgK)\n- c_v = specific heat at constant volume (kJ/kgK)\n\nThe ratio is dimensionless and has the same value in both SI and Imperial units."
